# Solve for Disappointment twice: the first makes the Jace token with one loyalty counter, the second finds it and puts its
# counter there instead of making another (CR 701.71a: a Jace token you control is chosen). At the end there is one Jace
# token with two loyalty counters, so the battlefield holds two Swamps, the Mox Jet and that token.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Solve for Disappointment
Swamp
Solve for Disappointment
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Llanowar Elves
Llanowar Elves
Llanowar Elves
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Solve for Disappointment.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Solve for Disappointment.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves; Llanowar Elves
